35,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found that our developers are busy with the accounting upgrade. We have no one to build this.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,I found that half the customer plants lose network coverage for whole afternoons. We cannot rely on live sync.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"I found that the capital line is frozen, but the software allowance still has room. We must buy, not build.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,I found that the last three rollouts failed because they needed daily entry from everyone. The narrow tools built for one trade still run.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found that we lose an hour a day copying records, and eleven deliveries went wrong because two units held different addresses.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@George, if we buy, does it still need someone to type the data in?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, if the network drops, the tool must work offline and sync later.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, a fixed-fee build is cheaper than a licence that climbs with every department added.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, the pattern is clear. We need a tool that one person can run, not one that needs everyone.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, that matches what I saw. The loss is in the copying, not in the thinking.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I am worried. If we buy a big tool, who types the data when the network is down?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. The tool must hold the data on the device and push it when the link returns.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,I agree. A fixed-fee build that one person runs fits the allowance and avoids the per-head climb.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,I agree. The last three failed because they asked everyone to type. The one that survived asked only one person.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree. If one person types the address once, the eleven misroutes stop and the hour of copying stops too.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I think we should pick the one that asks the least of the people.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I think we should pick the one that works when the link is down.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I think we should pick the one that fits the allowance and does not climb with headcount.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I think we should pick the one that one person can run, because that is the one that survived.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I think we should pick the one that stops the copying and the misroutes, because that is where the day is lost.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
