60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I am looking at the Field Service App. It lets the technician type once on the phone, and the note goes to the office.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I am looking at the Field Service App. It stores the job on the phone and pushes it when the link returns, so the afternoon drop does not lose the record.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"I am looking at the Field Service App. It is a fixed-fee build, so the bill does not climb with every department added, and it fits the software allowance.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"I am looking at the Field Service App. It asks one person to type the job, not everyone to type the status, so it follows the pattern of the tool that survived.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I am looking at the Field Service App. It stops the copying of the address and the job note, and it stops the misroute because the address is typed once and shared.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, does the app still work if the phone has no signal for a whole day?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Yes. The job, the photo, and the note stay on the phone and sync when the link returns.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Minato, the fixed-fee build means the bill is set at signing, not at every renewal.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, that is the pattern. The tool that survived was the one that did not need a new owner every quarter.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, that is the pattern I saw. The loss was in the copying, not in the thinking, and this stops the copying.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,I am still worried about the two people who write the weekly note. Will the app take that from them?,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"It drafts the note from the job record, so they check it instead of writing it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"I am satisfied. The bill is fixed, the allowance covers it, and the per-head climb is gone.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"I am satisfied. It asks one person to type the job, not everyone to type the status, so it follows the pattern of the tool that survived.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I am satisfied. It stops the hour of copying and the eleven misroutes, because the address is typed once and shared.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I will vote for the Field Service App, because it asks the least of the people and the note is drafted, not written.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I will vote for the Field Service App, because it works when the link is down and the record is not lost.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"I will vote for the Field Service App, because the bill is fixed, the allowance covers it, and the per-head climb is gone.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"I will vote for the Field Service App, because it asks one person to type the job, not everyone to type the status, so it follows the pattern of the tool that survived.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I will vote for the Field Service App, because it stops the copying and the misroutes, and that is where the day is lost.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
